IMPORT prelude

-- Transport Safety Investigations Act 2018 (Singapore) -- which transport occurrences the Act reaches (s 5), the duty to report them
-- (s 12), when the Transport Safety Investigation Bureau (TSIB) must or may investigate (ss 15, 16), draft and published reports
-- (ss 19, 21), the limits of the medical-examination power (s 29(4)), the offences and their penalties (ss 12, 13, 19, 22, 33-36, 43),
-- self-incrimination and the identification-card defence (ss 37, 38(1)), and the composition cap (s 42).
--
-- Edition: the deposit is the Act as enacted (it is headed "No. 36 of 2018" and cites other Acts by "Cap." numbers), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/TSIA2018.txt, with amendment annotations to Act 33 of 2021 (wef 10/04/2024, the definition of
-- "other proceedings") and Act 40 of 2019 ("General Division of the High Court" in s 43; annotated wef 10/01/2025, once as
-- 10/01/2015). The SSO metadata calls it the "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026". It is NOT labelled a 2020 Revised Edition.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what an operator, crew member, witness
-- or bystander meets: reach, reporting, the investigation trigger, reports and their evidential status, and the offences. Not
-- encoded: the TSIB's constitution and functions (ss 8-11), investigators' appointment and entry, search and seizure powers
-- (ss 23-28, 30, 31), cost recovery (s 18), reopening (s 17), corporate and partnership liability (ss 39, 40), the High Court
-- disclosure order (s 43(4), (5)), service (s 48), regulations, and the amendments to other Acts (Part 8). WHAT IS PRESCRIBED --
-- which occurrences are "immediately reportable", the reporting time, the prescribed particulars, which offences are compoundable --
-- is left to regulations that were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Transport Safety Investigations Act 2018 -- investigations`

-- s 2: "transport vehicle" means (a) an aircraft; (b) a ship; (c) a rail vehicle; or (d) a public passenger service motor vehicle
-- ("a motor vehicle when used to provide regular route services under a public bus services contract entered into with the LTA").
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF
    `an aircraft`
    `a ship`
    `a rail vehicle`
    `a public bus`

DECLARE Occurrence
    HAS `the mode` IS A Mode
        `happened in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a foreign authority asked Singapore to investigate or assist` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the aircraft holds a Singapore aviation safety instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the location cannot be established as in any country` IS A BOOLEAN
        `evidential material is found in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
        `involves a Singapore aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
        `involves a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN
        `involves another ship licensed under a law the MPA administers` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a witness arrives or is found in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
        `happened on or after the rail relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the rail vehicle runs on a railway wholly or partly in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the Minister ordered an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the Director considers it necessary and the foreign authority agrees` IS A BOOLEAN
        `Singapore has an international right or obligation to participate` IS A BOOLEAN
        `involves an exempt transport vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
        `involves a transport vehicle that is not exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
        `involves a civil transport facility` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is a flying display with the site outside military premises` IS A BOOLEAN
        `involves a Singapore military ship or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the Armed Forces asked the TSIB to investigate` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `5 -- what the Act reaches`

-- s 5(2): aviation occurrences "(a) in or over Singapore; or (b) in or over any place outside Singapore if -- (i) Singapore is
-- requested to investigate, or to participate or assist ... by an appropriate foreign authority; or (ii) the aviation occurrence --
-- (A) involves an aircraft in respect of which ... an aviation safety instrument is or has been issued under the Air Navigation Act;
-- and (B) is in a location which cannot be definitely established as being in the territory of any country and evidential material
-- ... is found in Singapore."
-- s 5(3): marine occurrences in Singapore, or outside if (i) a foreign request; (ii) "involves a Singapore ship or other ship licensed
-- under any written law administered by the MPA"; or (iii) "a witness to, or a person having information ... arrives or is found at
-- any place in Singapore".
-- s 5(4), (5): railway occurrences "happening on or after the relevant date" (a date the Minister specifies by order) in Singapore,
-- or outside on a foreign request.
-- s 5(6): "occurrences happening in Singapore involving the operation of a public passenger service motor vehicle" -- and nothing
-- outside Singapore.
GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN Occurrence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the occurrence`'s `the mode`
    WHEN `an aircraft` THEN
            `the occurrence`'s `happened in Singapore`
        OR  `the occurrence`'s `a foreign authority asked Singapore to investigate or assist`
        OR  (    `the occurrence`'s `the aircraft holds a Singapore aviation safety instrument`
             AND `the occurrence`'s `the location cannot be established as in any country`
             AND `the occurrence`'s `evidential material is found in Singapore`)
    WHEN `a ship` THEN
            `the occurrence`'s `happened in Singapore`
        OR  `the occurrence`'s `a foreign authority asked Singapore to investigate or assist`
        OR  `the occurrence`'s `involves a Singapore ship`
        OR  `the occurrence`'s `involves another ship licensed under a law the MPA administers`
        OR  `the occurrence`'s `a witness arrives or is found in Singapore`
    WHEN `a rail vehicle` THEN
            `the occurrence`'s `happened on or after the rail relevant date`
        AND (    `the occurrence`'s `happened in Singapore`
             OR  `the occurrence`'s `a foreign authority asked Singapore to investigate or assist`)
    WHEN `a public bus` THEN `the occurrence`'s `happened in Singapore`

§§ `16 -- which occurrences may be investigated`

-- s 16(1): "must not be investigated under this Act unless -- (a) it occurs in Singapore; (b) it involves -- (i) a Singapore aircraft;
-- (ii) a Singapore ship; (iii) a rail vehicle operating on a railway located wholly or partly in Singapore; or (iv) a public passenger
-- service motor vehicle operating within Singapore and an order is given under section 15(2)(b) ...; or (c) it occurs outside
-- Singapore and" (i) evidence is found in Singapore; (ii) a foreign authority requests; (iii) the Director considers it necessary
-- "and the agreement of the appropriate foreign authority is obtained"; or (iv) Singapore has "a right or an obligation, under an
-- international agreement, to participate or assist".
--
-- Limb (b)(iv) adds nothing: a bus "operating within Singapore" already occurs in Singapore under limb (a). Encoded as written.
GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN Occurrence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16(1) is met` IF
        `the occurrence`'s `happened in Singapore`
    OR  `the occurrence`'s `involves a Singapore aircraft`
    OR  `the occurrence`'s `involves a Singapore ship`
    OR  (`the occurrence`'s `the mode` EQUALS `a rail vehicle` AND `the occurrence`'s `the rail vehicle runs on a railway wholly or partly in Singapore`)
    OR  (`the occurrence`'s `the mode` EQUALS `a public bus` AND `the occurrence`'s `happened in Singapore` AND `the occurrence`'s `the Minister ordered an investigation`)
    OR  (    (NOT `the occurrence`'s `happened in Singapore`)
         AND (    `the occurrence`'s `evidential material is found in Singapore`
              OR  `the occurrence`'s `a foreign authority asked Singapore to investigate or assist`
              OR  `the occurrence`'s `the Director considers it necessary and the foreign authority agrees`
              OR  `the occurrence`'s `Singapore has an international right or obligation to participate`))

-- s 16(2): "Despite subsection (1), a transport occurrence cannot be investigated under this Act if -- (a) it involves, or relates to,
-- an exempt transport vehicle; (b) it does not involve, or relate to, any other transport vehicle that is not an exempt transport
-- vehicle; and (c) it does not involve, or relate to, a civil transport facility unless the occurrence is associated with a flying
-- display and the accident site is outside of military premises."
-- s 2: exempt transport vehicles are foreign military, customs and police aircraft and ships, Singapore military aircraft and vessels,
-- Government police, border-control and civil-defence vessels, and vessels wearing the State Marine Ensign.
-- s 16(3): "subsection (2) does not prevent an investigation of a transport occurrence that involves a Singapore military ship or
-- Singapore military aircraft if an appropriate authority in the Singapore Armed Forces requests".
--
-- READING (an inference): the "unless" clause in (c) is read as taking a flying display held outside military premises out of the
-- bar altogether, so that such an occurrence may be investigated even if only exempt (military) aircraft are involved.
GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN Occurrence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16(2) bars the investigation` IF
        `the occurrence`'s `involves an exempt transport vehicle`
    AND (NOT `the occurrence`'s `involves a transport vehicle that is not exempt`)
    AND (NOT `the occurrence`'s `involves a civil transport facility`)
    AND (NOT `the occurrence`'s `is a flying display with the site outside military premises`)
    AND (NOT (    `the occurrence`'s `involves a Singapore military ship or aircraft`
              AND `the occurrence`'s `the Armed Forces asked the TSIB to investigate`))

GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN Occurrence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occurrence may be investigated` IF
    `s 16(1) is met` `the occurrence` AND (NOT `s 16(2) bars the investigation` `the occurrence`)

§§ `15 -- when an investigation must be carried out`

-- s 15(1): "Subject to section 16, as soon as an immediately reportable matter has been notified ... and if the Director believes that
-- the circumstances ... (a) have, or are likely to have, significant implications for transport safety; and (b) may allow the TSIB to
-- establish findings or make recommendations which may improve transport safety, an investigation must be carried out".
-- s 15(2): the Director (a) "may" investigate any other notified occurrence; and (b) "must" investigate any occurrence "(whether or
-- not notified ...) if ordered in writing by the Minister".
-- s 15(4): "The Director may discontinue an investigation at any time except an investigation ... ordered by the Minister".
GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN Occurrence, `notified as immediately reportable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Director believes it has significant safety implications` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Director believes findings may improve safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an investigation must be carried out` IF
        `the occurrence may be investigated` `the occurrence`
    AND (    (    `notified as immediately reportable`
              AND `the Director believes it has significant safety implications`
              AND `the Director believes findings may improve safety`)
         OR  `the occurrence`'s `the Minister ordered an investigation`)

GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN Occurrence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may discontinue the investigation` IF
    NOT `the occurrence`'s `the Minister ordered an investigation`

§§ `12 -- the duty to report`

-- s 12(1): a responsible person (s 2: for an aircraft "the owner, operator and pilot-in-command", plus aerodrome operators and air
-- traffic service providers; for a ship "the owner, master and person-in-charge"; for a rail vehicle "the owner, operator and
-- driver"; for a bus, "such person as may be prescribed") who "has knowledge of an immediately reportable matter ... must report to a
-- nominated official within the time and by the means prescribed".
-- (2): for an ordinary reportable matter, only "if so required by the Director by notice in writing".
-- (3): neither applies "if the responsible person knows that another responsible person has ... already reported ... with all the
-- particulars required".
-- (4): "without reasonable excuse" -- a fine not exceeding $100,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 5 years or both.
DECLARE ReportableKind IS ONE OF
    `an immediately reportable matter`
    `an ordinary reportable matter`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A ReportableKind, `the Director required a report by notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the responsible person reported it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew another responsible person had already reported it in full` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to report is an offence` IF
        (    `the matter` EQUALS `an immediately reportable matter`
         OR  `the Director required a report by notice`)
    AND (NOT `the responsible person reported it`)
    AND (NOT `knew another responsible person had already reported it in full`)
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `19, 21 -- draft and published reports`

-- s 19(2): a person who receives a draft report "must not -- (a) make a copy of the whole or any part of the draft report; or
-- (b) disclose any of the contents ... to any other person or to a court". (3): $20,000 or 12 months or both.
-- (4): not "any copying or disclosure that is necessary for the purpose of -- (a) preparing submissions on the draft report; or
-- (b) taking steps to remedy safety issues that are identified in the draft report". No "reasonable excuse" defence is written.
GIVEN `copied or disclosed the draft report` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was necessary to prepare submissions` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it was necessary to remedy an identified safety issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `handling the draft report is an offence` IF
        `copied or disclosed the draft report`
    AND (NOT `it was necessary to prepare submissions`)
    AND (NOT `it was necessary to remedy an identified safety issue`)

-- s 21(1): a published report "is not admissible in evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings or other proceedings". (2): "However,
-- subsection (1) does not apply to a coroner's inquiry." (3): a draft report "is not admissible in evidence in any civil or criminal
-- proceedings or other proceedings" -- with NO coroner's exception.
-- s 2: "civil proceedings" are court proceedings other than criminal "and includes a coroner's inquiry"; "other proceedings" include
-- arbitration and employer disciplinary proceedings "but does not include proceedings in Parliament or a committee of Parliament".
DECLARE Proceeding IS ONE OF
    `a civil suit`
    `a criminal trial`
    `an arbitration`
    `an employer's disciplinary hearing`
    `a coroner's inquiry`
    `proceedings in Parliament`

DECLARE ReportStage IS ONE OF
    `a published report`
    `a draft report`

GIVEN `the report` IS A ReportStage, `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21 bars the report as evidence` IF
    CONSIDER `the proceeding`
    WHEN `proceedings in Parliament` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a coroner's inquiry` THEN `the report` EQUALS `a draft report`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `29(4) -- what a medical examination may involve`

-- s 29(4): the requirement to submit to a medical examination "does not extend to a requirement that the individual submit to any
-- procedure involving surgery or the injection into the body of any drug, but includes requiring the individual to undergo a
-- breath-analyser test or a toxicological examination or to provide blood or urine for a laboratory test".
DECLARE Procedure IS ONE OF
    `a breath-analyser test`
    `a toxicological examination`
    `a blood sample for a laboratory test`
    `a urine sample for a laboratory test`
    `a procedure involving surgery`
    `an injection of a drug`

GIVEN `the procedure` IS A Procedure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an investigator may require the procedure` IF
    CONSIDER `the procedure`
    WHEN `a procedure involving surgery` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an injection of a drug` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `33, 36, 37, 38 -- interfering with and refusing investigators`

-- s 33(1): an offence where the person engages in conduct, "knows that the conduct, or is reckless as to whether the conduct, will
-- adversely affect an investigation or a preliminary assessment that is being conducted at that time or that could be conducted at a
-- later time", the conduct "has the result of adversely affecting" it, and it "is not authorised by section 32, or by the Director or
-- an investigator". (2): $100,000 or 5 years or both.
-- s 32: nothing prevents conduct necessary to ensure the safety of persons, animals or property, remove the dead, move a vehicle or
-- wreckage to a safe place, protect the environment, or prevent danger or obstruction.
GIVEN `knew or was reckless that it would adversely affect an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the investigation was adversely affected` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised by s 32 or by the Director or an investigator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under s 33` IF
        `knew or was reckless that it would adversely affect an investigation`
    AND `the investigation was adversely affected`
    AND (NOT `authorised by s 32 or by the Director or an investigator`)

-- s 36(1)(a): an offence if the person, "without reasonable excuse -- (a) refuses to answer a question addressed to the person under
-- section 28". (3): $100,000 or 5 years or both.
-- s 37(1): "A person is not excused from answering a question ... on the ground that the answer ... might tend to incriminate the
-- person."
-- s 38(1): "It is not an offence under this Act for any person to refuse to comply with any requirement ... if the Director or
-- investigator -- (a) failed to comply with section 24(3)" (produce the identification card before exercising a power and on request)
-- "or (b) refused to produce his or her identification card on demand".
GIVEN `refused to answer an investigator's question` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the only ground is that the answer might incriminate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had some other reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the investigator produced an identification card as s 24(3) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing to answer is an offence` IF
        `refused to answer an investigator's question`
    AND (NOT `had some other reasonable excuse`)
    AND `the investigator produced an identification card as s 24(3) requires`

-- s 37(2): "Where a person, who is an individual, claims, before answering ... that the answer ... might tend to incriminate him or
-- her", the answer and anything obtained from it "are not admissible in evidence against that person in any civil proceedings or any
-- criminal proceedings in a court, other than proceedings for an offence ... in respect of the falsity of the answer". The protection
-- is for individuals only, and only if claimed BEFORE answering.
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `claimed the privilege before answering` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the proceeding is for the falsity of the answer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer is admissible against the person` IF
        (NOT `the person is an individual`)
    OR  `the proceeding is for the falsity of the answer`
    OR  (NOT `claimed the privilege before answering`)

§§ `Penalties and s 42 -- maxima and the composition cap`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 12 failing to report`
    `s 13 failing to give a required report`
    `s 19 copying or disclosing a draft report`
    `s 22 failing to respond to a safety recommendation`
    `s 33 adversely affecting an investigation`
    `s 34 hindering an investigation`
    `s 35 entering a cordoned-off area`
    `s 36 refusing to answer or give documents`
    `s 43 recording or disclosing restricted information`

-- ss 12(4), 13(2), 33(2), 36(3): $100,000 or 5 years. ss 19(3), 34(3), 43(6): $20,000 or 12 months. ss 22(4), 35(2): $10,000 or
-- 6 months. In every case "or to both".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 12 failing to report` THEN 100000
    WHEN `s 13 failing to give a required report` THEN 100000
    WHEN `s 19 copying or disclosing a draft report` THEN 20000
    WHEN `s 22 failing to respond to a safety recommendation` THEN 10000
    WHEN `s 33 adversely affecting an investigation` THEN 100000
    WHEN `s 34 hindering an investigation` THEN 20000
    WHEN `s 35 entering a cordoned-off area` THEN 10000
    WHEN `s 36 refusing to answer or give documents` THEN 100000
    WHEN `s 43 recording or disclosing restricted information` THEN 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the maximum fine` `the offence` EQUALS 100000
    THEN 60
    ELSE IF `the maximum fine` `the offence` EQUALS 20000
         THEN 12
         ELSE 6

-- s 42(1): the Director may compound "any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a compoundable offence". (2): "by collecting ...
-- a sum not exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence;
-- (b) $5,000." Which offences are compoundable is left to regulations (not retrieved). s 49(3)(a): regulations may create offences
-- with a fine not exceeding $100,000.
--
-- The smallest maximum fine for an offence in the Act is $10,000, half of which is $5,000: for every offence in the Act the $5,000
-- limb is the lower or equal one. Only an offence in regulations with a maximum below $10,000 could be compounded for less.
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `x` AT MOST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap for a maximum fine of` MEANS `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap` MEANS `the composition cap for a maximum fine of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence`)
